Statement: "With this code, one search_lessons result stays bounded (at most 20 items with 200-character snippets) however many lessons match the query."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'True. The handler clamps limit to the range 1..20 whatever the model asks for, cuts every snippet to 200 characters and never returns lesson bodies, so the size of one result has a fixed upper bound; the 5000 in the log was silently reduced to 20 and the rest is reachable through nextCursor, one bounded page at a time. Fetching limit + 1 rows is how the code knows whether a next page exists without counting every match. The misconception is that pagination only matters for the database; for an agent it also bounds the tokens a single tool result can push into the context window.', 2, 5
