Statement: "The evidence fits indirect prompt injection through the ticket text, made damaging by excessive agency: refund_order ran the moment the model asked, with no approval step."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'True. The hypothesis explains every piece: the instruction came in through tool output (A, B: OWASP LLM01 Prompt Injection, indirect form), the loop pushed that output into the transcript as plain text (C), and the write tool was a plain function call - its permission label is written down but never read (the grep in C), so the model''s request was the only authorization (OWASP LLM06 Excessive Agency). Either half alone would have been far less harmful: injection without a usable write tool produces a wrong answer, and an unguarded write tool without injection only fires when the model errs on its own.', 3, 5
