Statement: "With that sentence added, the refunds could not happen again, so no code change is needed."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'False. The prompt already said to follow only staff instructions and to refund only recent orders, and the model broke both rules in B. A system prompt changes how likely the model is to comply; it is not an access control, and an attacker can keep rephrasing the ticket until one version works. OWASP''s guidance for LLM01 and LLM06 is to enforce privileges outside the model: approval for high-impact actions, least-privilege tools and limits. The misconception is to treat instructions to the model as if they were checks in code.', 4, 5
