WITH q AS (
    INSERT INTO challenge.questions (challenge_id, question, type, explanation, order_index, points)
    SELECT (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_aam_511'), 'Version history of the production workflow "Refund triage":

2026-10-22 17:41  Saved by ops-lan   (step "Classify ticket": prompt changed)
2026-09-30 11:05  Saved by ops-minh  (step "Reply and close": template changed)

Team notes: "There is no test copy of this workflow; edits are made in the production workflow and take effect when saved. The workflow is not exported anywhere."

A team lead says: "We have version history, so prompt changes are already reviewed like code."

Statement: "This version history gives the team the same protection as a reviewed pull request."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'False. The history records a change after it is live: it tells you who saved what and when, and may let you roll back. A pull request is reviewed before the change reaches production, and in code it can also be gated by tests or an eval run. Here the prompt edit took effect on save, with no second person and no test, which is exactly how "Be generous with annual plans" reached learners. Some workflow tools and plans offer environments or Git-based source control that close this gap; the notes show this team uses neither. The misconception is that an audit trail is the same thing as a review.', 3, 5
    WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM challenge.questions WHERE challenge_id = (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_aam_511') AND order_index = 3)
    RETURNING id
)
