              mean   p50   p95   max
v14 (10-19)   4.1    3     6     12
v15 (10-21)   4.8    3     19    25

Statement: "The p95 shows a group of conversations that became much longer under v15, a change the mean understates."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'True. The median did not move and the mean rose by only 0.7 calls (about 17%), but the 95th percentile tripled from 6 to 19: at least 5% of conversations, several hundred a day, now take far more steps. That is where the extra tickets, tokens and latency come from. A mean blends a small group of very long runs with thousands of normal ones, so it hides the tail where agents fail. The misconception is that a small change in the average means a small change in behaviour; watch p95 and max against a baseline and alert on them.', 3, 5
    WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM challenge.questions WHERE challenge_id = (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_aam_531') AND order_index = 3)
    RETURNING id
)
